The alliance is a coalition of guests aboard the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], gathered when the [[Phenomena/Pilgrimage|pilgrimage]]'s tithe rose and the smaller Orgs found they could not each pay it. Its seat is the Heart [[Org/Iconoclasm/Eerie|Eerie]] at berth 14, which the member Orgs share. The smaller members give up their own Hearts to it: their fanes are left behind and the energy is fed to Eerie, so that the alliance holds one Heart instead of many.

[[Org/Alkahest Freight/index|Alkahest Freight]] and [[Org/Solari Sub-surface/index|Solari Sub-surface]] joined outright, and their people moved to berth 14; the [[Org/Protectorate/index|Protectorate]] took over the berths and territory they left. [[Org/Radiant Arms/index|Radiant Arms]] first joined while keeping its own Heart and berth; it has since given up its Heart to Eerie and moved its people to berth 14. [[Org/Prime Meridian/index|Prime Meridian]], the [[Org/The Scale/index|Scale]], the [[Org/Hildebrandt Corporation/index|Hildebrandt Corporation]] and the Protectorate stand with the alliance without merging, and the Party pays the difference in the tithe for those that ask it.

Members swear three things: to protect the coalition's Heart and everyone in it, to do harm to none of their fellows, and to hold no other allegiance ahead of the coalition. The Party hears the pledges through [[People/Argyle|Argyle]]'s Ring of Truth, and calls the document the Strider Accords.

The Party's people have taken to calling the alliance the Coalition, a plain name for a company drawn from different parts, and keep the name Heartbreakers for their own four.

The Party speaks for the coalition in practice. When the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]] stopped and the member Orgs began clamoring for answers, they came to the Party to call them together, and the Party's berth is where the coalition's plans are made.

Since the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]] halted, the Party has spoken for the coalition in a truce with [[Org/Amber Call/People/Silven Grayson|Silven Grayson]] of [[Org/Amber Call/index|Amber Call]] and [[Org/Iridescent Church/People/Walter Stoke|Walter Stoke]] of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]]. The three sides keep off one another's ground and meet at [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Giacomo's|Giacomo's]], which the whole central circle about the strider's tower is named neutral and safe.
